    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="73ae7fe2-20cf-5fe8-92c4-a886916f422b" activityNameId="9777d187-760f-5222-b542-eb96bff78ccc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ground heat exchanger for appartment buildings, PE ducts</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ground heat exchanger for appartment buildings, PE ducts
Disposal of a ground heat exchanger for an appartment building with a specific air flow rate of 0.92 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. The reference value of the inventory is 1 m2 heated gross floor area. The inventory is based on a study of an appartment building with 6 flats, a heated gross floor area of 780 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 720 m3/h. The inventory includes a ground heat exchanger with 200mm diameter and a lenght of 0.154m/m2. The data represents a ground heat exchanger made of polyethylene. It includes the excavating needed and a bedding layer made of poor concrete.;
UUID: db4c854e-518e-4adc-81d8-fb7638a93806
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Process information partly from 2008. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_db4c854e-518e-4adc-81d8-fb7638a93806.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
